# compute probability estimates under model M1 pred.1 = predict(m.1,type = &#34;response&#34;) prob.table = matrix(c(pred.1),nrow = 4) dimnames(prob.table) = list(c(&#34;science male&#34;,&#34;science female&#34;, &#34;non-science male&#34;,&#34;non-science female&#34;), c(&#34;prob.1&#34;)) print(prob.table,digits = 4) ## prob.1 ## science male 0.8667 ## science female 0.8667 ## non-science male 0.5814 ## non-science female 0.5814 Under model $M_1$, we estimate the probability of admission into the science department is $0.8667$ and we estimate probability of admission into the non-science department is $0.5814$.
